   **Quote from retrieved review (EIXZXPz7jU)**: "While the experimental evaluation on the chosen dataset is comprehensive, I believe the paper would benefit from evaluation on an additional dataset. This would improve the paper, evaluating [the method] across different data distributions and characteristics."

2. **Insufficient ablation studies**: The paper lacks comprehensive ablation studies to isolate the contributions of different components (regularized mirror map vs. Student-t prior). While Figure 3 shows performance for different κ and ν values, there is no systematic ablation comparing: (i) regularized mirror map with Gaussian prior, (ii) standard log-barrier with Student-t prior, (iii) the full proposed method.

   **Quote from retrieved review (LyJi5ugyJx)**: "The advantage of LFM on fast training has not been demonstrated well except Table 2... More details should be provided, such as the number of function evaluations (NFEs) and the used ODE sampler for all methods in Table 1 and Table 2, to better demonstrate [the method's] effectiveness."
   
