## WEAKNESSES

**1. Insufficient Complexity Analysis and Computational Cost Discussion**

The paper lacks thorough time and space complexity analysis when integrating the proposed lightweight components with baseline models. While TSPulse is described as "lightweight" with 1M parameters, reviewers of similar papers consistently point out that such claims require detailed complexity analysis.

> "When the predictor is a linear model, the complexity of PTN seems to far exceed that of the predictor itself. It is suggested to provide the time and memory complexity analysis of the proposed module." (Review of 6hJ3khuJY4, Reviewer 1)

> "The paper lacks a detailed analysis of time and computational costs, particularly a comparison between the original base model and the model combined with MADCluster." (Review of Tepaft7632, Reviewer 3)

**2. Limited Ablation Studies on Disentangled Components**

The paper proposes three complementary embedding views (temporal, spectral, semantic), but may lack sufficient ablation studies demonstrating the independent contribution of each component to the overall performance gain, particularly across different task types.

> "The paper lacks a detailed analysis of time and computational costs, particularly a comparison between the original base model and the model combined with MADCluster...No ablation study for learnable cluster center and one-directed adaptive loss?" (Review of Tepaft7632, Reviewer 1)

**3. Baseline Comparisons May Lack Fairness**

TSPulse compares against larger models (10-100x larger), but reviewers of comparable papers consistently note concerns about whether baselines are tested under equivalent conditions (e.g., same hyperparameters, same experimental settings, same look-back windows).

> "The comparison with baselines in Table 9 for look-back length 512 appears to be unfair. For instance, iTransformer should also use a look-back length of 512, and the results of PatchTST in this table are much worse than those reported in the PatchTST paper." (Review of 6hJ3khuJY4, Reviewer 4)

**4. Limited Evaluation on Complex and Diverse Datasets**

While TSPulse reports results on 75+ datasets, reviewers of time-series papers consistently point out that performance on simple/linear datasets may not generalize equally to complex, non-stationary, or real-world datasets.

> "The proposed model does not seem to perform well on complex datasets, such as Traffic. It would be beneficial to provide results on more complex datasets, such as the PEMS datasets used in the iTransformer paper." (Review of 6hJ3khuJY4, Reviewer 4)

**5. Missing Comparison with Recent Pre-trained Foundation Models**

The paper may lack comprehensive comparison with other recent time-series pre-trained models beyond those mentioned in related work. Reviewers consistently expect comparison with all state-of-the-art pre-trained methods.

> "More comparison with the pretrained methods for TS anomaly detection should be discussed, such as TimesNet and FPT." (Review of Tepaft7632, Reviewer 1)

**6. Unclear Implementation Details for Reproducibility**

While the authors claim to provide "publicly available" models and code, reviews consistently raise concerns about missing implementation details, hyperparameter selection rationale, and reproducibility information.

> "The empirical results seem to be very surprising in my opinion. I encourage authors to add their code and provide clear guidelines to reproduce it." (Review of dIaykjbiiL, Reviewer 1)

## STRENGTHS

**1. Comprehensive Multi-Task Evaluation Framework**

The paper evaluates the model across four distinct diagnostic tasks (anomaly detection, imputation, similarity search, classification), demonstrating broad applicability beyond single-task forecasting.

> "The proposed method achieves state-of-the-art performance on seven real-world datasets. The ablation experiments are comprehensive." (Review of 6hJ3khuJY4, Reviewer 1)

**2. Novel Disentangled Representation Approach**

The explicit disentanglement across temporal, spectral, and semantic spaces represents a principled approach to multi-view representation learning that goes beyond simply learning joint embeddings.

> "The core idea is creative, making use of the wealth of longitudinal EHR data associated with each 3D volume for pretraining." (Review of zcTLpIfj9u, Reviewer 3)

**3. Efficient Model Architecture for Deployment**

The ultra-lightweight 1M parameter model that supports GPU-free deployment addresses real practical constraints in edge computing and resource-constrained environments.
